hadiths[42]{hadithnumber,text}:
"488","Abu Hurairah narrated that:the Prophet said: \The best day that the sun has risen upon is Friday. On it Adam was created"""
"489","Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Prophet said: \Seek out the hour that is hoped for on Friday after Asr until the sun has set"""
"490","Kathir bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Awf Al-Muzani narrated from his father"
"491","Abu Hurairah narrated:\Allah's Messenger said: The best day that the sun has risen upon is Friday. On it Adam was created"""
"492","It was narrated to us by Ahmad ibn Mani', who narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Az-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \Whoever attends the Friday prayer"
"493","Salim narrated:(Another chain) from Abdullah bin Umar from the Prophet which is similar"
"494","Abū ʿĪsā said: It has also been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar, from ʿUmar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding the ritual bath (ghusl) on Friday. This is a hasan sahih hadith. It was narrated by Yūnus and Maʿmar from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from his father: While ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb was delivering the sermon on Friday, a man from among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) entered. ʿUmar asked, \What time is this [that you have come]?\"" The man replied"
"495","(Another chain reaching to Az-Zuhri) with this Hadith.Malik reported this Hadith from Az-Zuhri"
"496","Aws bin Aws narrated:\Allah's Messenger said to me: 'Whoever performs Ghusl on Friday"""
"497","Samurah bin Jundah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever performs Wudu on Friday"""
"498","Abu Hurairh narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever performs Wudu"""
"499","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever performs Ghusl on Friday - the Ghusl for Janabah - then he goes"""
"500","**Narrated by ʿAlī ibn Khashram:** He informed us that ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus reported from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, from ʿAbīdah ibn Sufyān, from Abū al-Jaʿd — meaning al-Ḍamrī — who was, as Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr claimed, a Companion (ṣāḥābī). He said:\n\n**The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:**\n\n> *\Whoever abandons the Friday prayer (Jumuʿah) three times out of negligence"
"501","**Narrated by 'Abd ibn Humayd and Muhammad ibn Maddūyah** — they both said: **Fadl ibn Dukayn** narrated to us: **Isrā'īl** narrated to us, from **Thuwayr**, from **a man from the people of Qubā'**, from **his father**, who was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n> \The Prophet ﷺ commanded us to attend the Friday prayer (al-Jumu'ah) from Qubā'.\""\n\n**It has also been narrated from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ regarding this matter"
"502","Narrator not mentioned:I heard Ahmad bin Husain saying: \We were with Ahmad bin Hanbal"""
"503","Anas bin Malik narrated:\The Prophet would pray the Friday prayer when the sun was declining"""
"504","**Yahya ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān narrated from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Taymī, from Anas رضي الله عنه, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it.**\n\nHe (Abū ʿĪsā) said: **\And in this chapter (there are narrations) from Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ"
"505","Ibn Umar narrated:\The Prophet would give the Khutbah next to the trunk of a date palm. When he [the Prophet] began using the Minbar the trunk cried out for him until he came to it and held it"""
"506","Ibn Umar narrated:\The Prophet would give a Khutbah on Friday"""
"507","**Qutaybah and Hannād narrated to us, both saying:** Abū al-Ahwāṣ narrated to us, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from Jābir ibn Samurah رضي الله عنه, who said:\n\n*\I used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ"
"508","Safwan bin Ya'la bin Umayyah narrated from his father who said:\I heard the Prophet reciting"""
"509","Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:\When Allah's Messenger descending the Minbar he would face our direction"""
"510","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:\The Prophet was delivering a Khutbah on Friday when a man came. The Prophet said: 'Have you prayed?' He said no. So he said: 'Then stand and pray.'\"" Abu Eisa said: This Hadith is Hasan Sahih [It is the most correct thing about this topic]"""
"511","Iyad bin Abdullah bin Abi Sarh narrated:\Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri entered (the mosque) on Friday while Marwan was giving the Khutbah"""
"512","Abu Hurairah narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever said: 'Be quiet' while the Imam is giving the Khutbah then he has committed Laghw (useless activity)"""
"513","Sahl bin Ma'adh bin Anas al Jahni narrated from his father that :Allah's Messenger said: \Whoever steps over the necks of the people on Friday"""
"514","Sahl bin Ma'adh narrated from his father:\The Prophet prohibited Al-Habwah on Friday while the Imam is delivering the Khutbah"""
"515","Husain narrated:\I heard Umarah bin Rawaibah Ath-Thaqafi - while Bishr bin Marwan was delivering Khutbah and raising his hands in supplication - so Umarah said: 'May Allah disgrace these two insignificant hands"""
"516","As-Sa'ib bin Yazid narrated:\The Adhan during the time of Allah's Messenger"""
"517","Anas bin Malik narrated:\Allah's Messenger would talk as necessary after descending from the Minbar"""
"518","Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Khallāl narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, Maʿmar informed us, from Thābit, from Anas رضي الله عنه, who said: \I saw the Prophet ﷺ"
"519","Ubaidullah bin Abi Rafi the freed slave of Allah's Messenger said:\Marwan left Abu Hurairah in charge of Al-Madinah and he went to Makkah. So Abu Hurairah led us in Salat in Friday"""
"520","Narrated by Ali ibn Hujr, who reported from Sharik, from Mukhawil ibn Rashid, from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'eed ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday Surah Al-Sajdah (Surah 32) and Surah Al-Insan (Surah 76).\n\nHe (the narrator) said: In this chapter, there are narrations from Sa'd, Ibn Mas'ud, and Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with them).\n\nAbu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: The hadith of Ibn Abbas is a hasan sahih hadith. It was also narrated by Sufyan al-Thawri, Shu'bah, and others from Mukhawil."
"521","Salim narrated from his father:\The Prophet would pray two Rak;ah after the Friday prayer"""
"522","Nafi narrated about Ibn Umar:\When he prayed the Friday prayer"""
"523","Ibn Abi Umar narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever among you prays after Jumu'ah, let him pray four."" Abu Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. Al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, who said: ""We used to consider Suhayl ibn Abi Salih trustworthy in hadith."" The practice is upon this according to some people of knowledge. It is narrated from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud that he used to pray four before Jumu'ah and four after it. It has been narrated from Ali ibn Abi Talib (ra) that he commanded that two rak'ahs be prayed after Jumu'ah, then four. Sufyan al-Thawri and Ibn al-Mubarak went with the view of Ibn Mas'ud. Ishaq said: If he prays in the mosque on the day of Jumu'ah, he prays four; if he prays in his house, he prays two. He cited as evidence that the Prophet ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs after Jumu'ah in his house, and the hadith of the Prophet ﷺ: ""Whoever among you prays after Jumu'ah, let him pray four."" Abu Isa said: Ibn Umar is the one who narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he used to pray two rak'ahs after Jumu'ah in his house. After the Prophet ﷺ, Ibn Umar prayed in the mosque after Jumu'ah two rak'ahs, then prayed four after the two rak'ahs. Ibn Abi Umar narrated this to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Ata, who said: ""I saw Ibn Umar pray after Jumu'ah two rak'ahs, then pray four after that."" Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar, who said: ""I have not seen anyone more precise in hadith than al-Zuhri, and I have not seen anyone to whom dinars and dirhams are lighter than him; if dinars and dirhams were with him, they were like dung."" Abu Isa said: I heard Ibn Abi Umar say: I heard Sufyan ibn Uyaynah say: ""Amr ibn Dinar was older than al-Zuhri."""
"524","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: \Whoever catches a Rak'ah of the Salat then he has caught the Salat"""
"525","Sahl bin Sa'd narrated:\We would not have lunch during the time of Allah's Messenger"""
"526","Ibn Umar narrated that :the Prophet said: \When one of you becomes sleepy during the Friday prayer"""
"527","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet sent Abdullah bin Rawahah to lead a military detachment"""
"528","Al-Bara bin Azib narrated that :Allah's Messenger said: \It is a duty for the Muslims"""
"529","Al-Bara bin Azib narrated:(Another route for the same chain) similar in meaning"
